-- title:
--   Unit times distinguished polynomial in a Drinfeld chart
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $W$ a local commutative ring whose maximal ideal is principal, generated by $\pi$, and let $f,u,v$ be formal power series in two variables $X_0,X_1$ over $W$ with $v$ a unit and with $f$ congruent to the Drinfeld form $X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$. Write $S$ for the quotient of $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ by the principal ideal generated by $\pi v-fu$ (the constant $\pi$ being viewed in the power series ring), and let $s\in S$ be a unit. Let $d,k$ be natural numbers and let $h\in(X_0,X_1)^d$ be such that for all $a,b\in W$ with at least one of $a,b$ outside the maximal ideal and with $a^qb-ab^q$ in the maximal ideal, the value $\sum_{i=0}^{d}\operatorname{coeff}_{(i,\,d-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{d-i}$ of the degree-$d$ homogeneous part of $h$ is a unit of $W$. Let $P\in W[X]$ be monic of degree $k$ with $P$'s $i$-th coefficient in $\mathfrak m_W^{\lfloor (k-i)d/(q+1)\rfloor+1}$ for every $i<k$. Then there exists $h'\in(X_0,X_1)^{dk}$ whose degree-$dk$ homogeneous part satisfies the same unit condition (with $d$ replaced by $dk$), such that in $S$ one has $s\cdot P(\bar h)=\overline{h'}$, where $P$ is mapped to $S[X]$ coefficientwise through the constants of the power series ring followed by the quotient map.
--
--   This is a Weierstrass-preparation statement for the Drinfeld local chart: multiplying a unit by a distinguished polynomial evaluated at an element of $(X_0,X_1)^d$ with everywhere-nonvanishing leading form again yields, modulo $\pi v-fu$, an element of $(X_0,X_1)^{dk}$ with nonvanishing leading form; it generalises the pure-power case $P=X^k$. It is used in the analysis of completed stalks of full-level modular curves at supersingular points, where the relevant parameter differs from a lift by a unit times a distinguished polynomial rather than a pure power.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart_exists_mem_pow_isUnit_homogeneous_mul_eval_map_eq_mk_of_monic.lean

